{:edb/db-before-t 1464 :edb/db-after-t 1465 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534777 50 #inst "2026-10-12T12:26:56.609Z" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186231427 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435715 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186231427 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435717 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186231428 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435716 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186231428 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435719 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186231429 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435718 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186231429 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435720 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186317433 1071 "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The particle is acted on by an external periodic force\n$f(t)=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t).$\nAssuming the system experiences resonance, which of the following could be used to represent the general solution for the position $y(t)?$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R,$ and $ϕ$ are constants." 13194139534777 17592186045417 false] [17592186317433 1071 "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The particle is acted on by an external periodic force\n$f(t)=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t).$\nAssuming the system experiences resonance, which of the following could be used to represent the general solution for the position $y(t)?$\n\nI. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nII. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nIII. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R,$ and $ϕ$ are constants." 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186317433 1074 "Because the motion is undamped and the system experiences resonance, the forcing frequency equals the natural frequency $\\omega .$\n\nThe external force is $f(t)=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t),$ which is sinusoidal with frequency $3.$ Therefore,\n$\\omega =3.$\n\nThe complementary solution for the associated simple harmonic motion equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nAt resonance, a sinusoidal trial at frequency $\\omega $ duplicates the complementary solution, so we multiply by $t$ and take a resonant particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution and $\\omega =3$ into the differential equation, ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[(6D-9Ct)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-(6C+9Dt)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)]+9t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) & =10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ 6D\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-6C\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & =10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, $C=0$ and $D=\\frac{5}{3}.$ \n\nSo, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nSolutions I, II, and III match the forms above.\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." 13194139534777 17592186045417 false] [17592186317433 1074 "Because the motion is undamped and the system experiences resonance, the forcing frequency equals the natural frequency $\\omega .$\n\nThe external force is $f(t)=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t),$ which is sinusoidal with frequency $3.$ Therefore,\n$\\omega =3.$\n\nThe complementary solution for the associated simple harmonic motion equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nAt resonance, a sinusoidal trial at frequency $\\omega $ duplicates the complementary solution, so we multiply by $t$ and take a resonant particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution and $\\omega =3$ into the differential equation, ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[(6D-9Ct)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-(6C+9Dt)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)]+9t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) & =10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ 6D\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-6C\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & =10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, $C=0$ and $D=\\frac{5}{3}.$ \n\nSo, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n1\\. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n2\\. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n3\\. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nSolutions I, II, and III match the forms above.\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435687 1080 "II only" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435687 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435687 1083 #uuid "0155fefb-60d8-5dc5-9cb9-bfd9b44bc962" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435688 1080 "I and III only" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435688 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435688 1083 #uuid "04294cfb-cb8e-5e85-95b0-be9065b6019e" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435689 1080 "III only" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435689 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435689 1083 #uuid "09521a1d-0037-59a4-b1e8-2b8b60a1d4de" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435690 1080 "II only" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435690 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435690 1083 #uuid "10aed726-550b-5773-a3d2-e5a9aa903d37" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435691 1080 "I only" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435691 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435691 1083 #uuid "23ab143c-f45b-5e8a-9480-58f173ceacfb" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435692 1080 "p=\\frac{5}{6}" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435692 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435692 1083 #uuid "3cf6a1db-f3c4-58d1-858e-32954c0da8e2" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435693 1080 "I and III only" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435693 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435693 1083 #uuid "4d110980-6336-5008-851d-def1533281f1" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435694 1080 "p=2" 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [17592186435694 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534777 17592186045417 true] [1759218643